# A deliberately ASYMMETRIC wedge, authored Z-UP (Blender convention).
#
# Hand-written, and ours, so it can live in a public repo. It exists because
# every downloaded fixture is authored Y-up in metres and therefore cannot
# exercise the axis-correction path at all -- the corrections were only ever
# tested against synthetic in-memory scenes, which is one of the two gaps a
# pair of silent geometry bugs fell through.
#
# OBJ carries no axis metadata, so a manifest declaring an explicit frame is
# the only thing that says which way is up. That makes this the smallest
# honest end-to-end test of "declare the frame once, in data".
#
# Shape: 4 m along source +Z (which must become engine +Y), 1 m along source
# +X, 2 m along source +Y (which must become engine -Z). Every axis a
# different length, so a wrong mapping cannot hide.
v 0.0 0.0 0.0
v 1.0 0.0 0.0
v 0.0 2.0 0.0
v 0.0 0.0 4.0
f 1 3 2
f 1 2 4
f 1 4 3
f 2 3 4
